/**
 * dsh-theme-p3r - Client half.
 *
 * A fan-made, asset-free skin in the Persona 3 Reload idiom: midnight navy,
 * electric blue, cyan hairlines, a HUD time scale along the bottom edge, a
 * 00:00 MEMENTO MORI readout, and dialogue laid out the way the game does it -
 * your line in a white box with blue ink, the answer in a blue box with white. Nothing from the game is bundled, traced or
 * referenced - every shape below is drawn here as CSS geometry, and the one
 * piece of artwork in the theme is a GIF the user supplied.
 *
 * Three layers, in this order:
 *   1) theme.overrideTokens - the app's own --dsw-alias-* tokens, light and dark
 *      pairs, so surfaces the app paints itself follow the palette and follow
 *      the OS light/dark switch with no JS repaint.
 *   2) the --dsw-static-neutral-* ramp, re-tinted to a blue-neutral scale, so
 *      components that reach for a raw step instead of an alias land in the
 *      same water instead of staying warm grey.
 *   3) one scoped stylesheet under body[data-p3r] - geometry (square corners,
 *      cyan hairlines, a clock ring), typography, scrollbar, selection, hover
 *      and enter motion. Scoped so that removing the attribute and the style
 *      element restores the stock UI exactly.
 *
 * The background GIF is inlined (see tools/sync-media.mjs) because a theme's
 * host half never activates on this build: /theme-p3r/media/* would 404. It is
 * handed to the page as an <img> layer rather than a CSS background so it can
 * be blurred - the source is 400x225 and stretching it to a 1440-wide window
 * without a blur would read as a mistake.
 *
 * Settings live nowhere: the plugin's presence is the switch. Uninstall or
 * disable the bundle to get the stock look back.
 */
